A||||19||2M4 Dale||RS Motorsports Sub-woofer Box||||14||
Z||000000||2M4 Dale||05-07-2000||11:01 AM||||Just finished installing it. Fit and finish on the center console sub-box is very nice. The thing allmost looks like a factory install. Used a Power Acoustic FB-8W 8" sub with a Pheonix Saphire Gold 35w amp. I put a Radio Shack waffle style grill over the sub. (really didn't want to cover it up BUT....)<BR>RS Motorsports list this box as having .4 air volume. I think this is optomistic at best. The woofer I used is very crisp sounding and gives me all the THUMP I need.<BR>For the head unit I used a Jenson AM/FM-cass with CD controls (1 1/2 din) and a 6 disk Jenson changer. Speakers are 4X10 Kenwoods with base blockers in the dash and 4X6 Kenwood excellons in the sails.<BR>Allthough this setup may not win any competitions I think it sounds GREAT !!!<P>RS Motorsports sub-box....Thumbs Up !!!http://webhome.idirect.com/~rsm1/<P>Special Thanks to StillofKnight for the woofer, amp and the installation !<P>[This message has been edited by 2M4 Dale (edited 05-07-2000).]<p>[This message has been edited by 2M4 Dale (edited 05-08-2000).]||||reg||14
Z||000001||Haze_Performance||05-07-2000||04:11 PM||||pics,pics,pics....we need to see the install...stop teasing us... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> ||||reg||10
Z||000002||Haze_Performance||05-07-2000||04:27 PM||||Im just wondering?? If the Sub is a free air, then why is the console in this picture so deep?<BR> <A HREF="http://webhome.idirect.com/~rsm1/speaker.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://webhome.idirect.com/~rsm1/speaker.jpg</A> <P>I know it has to be alittle big to fit the magnet + the computer, But it still looks to large for a free air.. It also looks like your arm would be very uncomfortable (If you tried to use the armrest)..<P>Ok im done....    <P>||||reg||10
Z||000003||Gokart||05-07-2000||08:32 PM||||Not a bad idea I guess for the limited space in our cars, but to me it's a theft/break in waiting to happen so visibly seen. I bet the speaker will dry out and crack eventually as well because it's constantly getting direct sunlight.||||reg||1
Z||000004||2birds||05-07-2000||09:30 PM||||So does the computer have to be moved to create the air space or what?<P>I built an upright sealed box .5 cu ft, about 6" deep, and it sits behind the pass seat, with it almost all the way forward.  Looks like a package tray behind the seat.  I have a 250 Watt amp driving an 8" JBL Sub, and it's perfect for me.  Nice and clear, good for anything from Buddy Guy to Metallica.  ||||reg||1
Z||000005||stillofknight||05-07-2000||11:32 PM|||| The sub is not a freeair sub. It is a low "Q" subwoofer optimized for small enclosures. The woofer will NOT be affected at all by sunlight. It has a butyl rubber surround, and polypropylene cone. It has a 50 oz. magnet, which is big for an 8" sub, but it fit fine in the box. The computer does NOT have to be moved. And as far as a break in, who is going to risk going to jail for 1 8" woofer. Not many people I suspect.<BR>P.S. If anyone is thinking of getting this enclosure, DO NOT buy a free air sub. You want a sub suited for a small sealed enclosure. ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Homicidal||05-08-2000||01:11 AM||||Who says they will goto jail?  Not everybody who steals the car gets caught.<P>If you want to cover it up, get a small peice of plastic or rubber that can just fall over it to make it not look so apparent.<P>2birds:<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.members.home.net/silksteel/Mvc-011s.jpg"> <P>I did the same, except mine is a 10" sub.  <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||stillofknight||05-08-2000||02:21 AM|||| Are you kidding? 2M4 Dale has a stock looking console with a metal mesh grill covering his sub. This picture is of a huge box sitting on the passenger seat of a Fiero with wires coming out of it. It isn't even mounted. Talk about an invitation to break into your car. Please tell me you don't ride around with a sub on your passenger seat!||||reg||1
Z||000008||2M4 Dale||05-08-2000||06:28 AM||||I'll post some pics in a day or two. Gotta finish cleaning the interior and put the passenger seat back in. As far as elbow room goes, I really don't notice the difference. The sub-box does NOT interfear with my elbow. And like StillofKnight said you have to use a low Q sub. This is a sealed box.<P>As far as the theft thing goes...Next on my agenda is some kind of security system. I'm really never to far from my car anyway...even at work.||||reg||1
Z||000009||phillip||05-08-2000||10:38 AM||||how much is the box, not including speaker and install? is it color matched already?<P>depending on how thick the speaker mounting area is maybe it could be routed out a little so the sub sits flush with the front mounting surface. then maybe make a square grill that looked more like the door that was there before.<p>[This message has been edited by phillip (edited 05-08-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000010||2birds||05-08-2000||04:43 PM||||Homicidal,<P>My box is a bit thinner, around 5.5" total, and a bit taller.  I covered it with some cheap grey flannel-like carpet from Home Depot, that is a perfect match for the firewall carpet, and it sits behind the pass seat, so you wouldn't even know it's there.  If I was to do it again, I'd taper it toward the bottom, so it would sit about two inches lower, and I'd also make the top sit level, instead of angled toward the back. <BR> My first serious attempt at woodworking...||||reg||1
Z||000011||Homicidal||05-08-2000||05:02 PM||||So is it mounted INSIDE the firewall or just right behind the seat?<P><BR>Stillofknight:  No, it is mounted BEHIND my seat, it is only on the seat for the pic and because I was cleaning the car.  ||||reg||1
Z||000012||2birds||05-08-2000||05:17 PM||||Mine's behind the seat.  Seat is almost all the way forward.  Legroom for the passenger is lost, but my wife is only 5'4", and my kids are 5 and 2, so no big deal.||||reg||1
Z||000013||Homicidal||05-08-2000||07:10 PM||||Ahh, what we do for sound!<P>BTW, I found out if I use a small "spacer" (wadded up peice of cardboard) to tilt my speaker around 1/2" away from the firewall, I get AWESOME bass since the waves have somewhere to go.  Cool discovery!||||reg||1
Z||000014||86SE||05-08-2000||09:00 PM||||My sub box is about the same size as yours homicidal!!<P>My box fits in the passenger footwell, absolutely NO room for the passengers feet so im going to have to make the box taller but narrower.<P>I have my sub box suspended above the floor (sub facing toward the floor) by about 3.5" to get hella sound and bass responce!!  Wow, waht a differance 3 inches makes!||||reg||10
Z||000015||stillofknight||05-08-2000||11:41 PM|||| Whew! I was hoping no one was riding around with that thing on their seat. I am surprised that a couple of you are actually willing to give up leg room for bass. Most people think that is absurd. But if you don't need the space, why not put a sub in? Sounds good to me.||||reg||1
Z||000016||2M4 Dale||05-09-2000||12:11 AM||||Phillip,<P>The box is NOT CHEAP. It cost $190.00 including shipping from Canada to Ohio. Plus you have to send them your old console as a core.<P>The front plate is about an 1" thick so I think (depending on speaker mount plate thickness) you could route it out and put a square grill over it. You might want to add some poly-fill to trick your speaker into thinking that the box is a little bigger. I didn't and my speaker sounds just fine. (You have to use a low Q speaker)<P>The reason I went with such an expensive box is two fold. It adds a neat custom touch to the interior and it takes up absolutly no room behind of either seat. I do plan to add a aftermarket glove box later. Like the one that the Fiero Store sells. Also the 8" sub and smallish amp are just right for my taste in music. It adds some THUMP without being obnoxious.<P>As far as the covering goes...I think you can order what you want. Mine is the darker gray color. Not light gray or charcoal. I really should have ordered charcoal...OH WELL <p>[This message has been edited by 2M4 Dale (edited 05-09-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000017||spike||05-09-2000||08:46 AM||||Is that 190 us or cdn.||||reg||1
Z||000018||2M4 Dale||05-09-2000||12:06 PM||||Thats good old U.S. greenbacks||||reg||1
Z||000019||spike||05-09-2000||01:48 PM||||So the console does not come with a Sub. 190.00 US for the box only. I would have built one myself and saved 140.00 US. I think this price is crazy and I would never pay that amount of money. <P>Here is some info about my box:<P>1. It takes 30 seconds to install/uninstall.<BR>2. Comes covered in matching vynle.<BR>3. Custom fit.<BR>4. Loss of 1.25 inch seat travel.<BR>5. Ready to drop in 2 10 inch Subs.<BR>6. Less then 190.00 US.<P>This box is not yet on the market but will be soon.<P>I will be attending various Fiero Shows this summer. I will bring about 6-8 boxes to each show.<P>Is there a place where I can get all info related to Fiero upcomming events.<P>I live in Montreal, Canada so the distance may cause a problem. My mother lives in Burlington, Vermont. What I might do is pay her a visit, build my boxes at her house and ship them from there. This should help avoid any Border problems.<P>Tks. Mike.<P>||||reg||1
